1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,857
PS hunting effort to make this cleanup

2
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:11,077
I'll see you

3
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:18,160
next

4
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:28,070
time.

5
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:45,320
Retreat! Retreat!

6
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:48,877
All Marines, evacuate!

7
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,300
Board your ships now!

8
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:53,297
Do you know what happened
at the center of the city?

9
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:54,340
No clue.

10
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:56,189
I'm just following orders.

11
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:05,070
St.

12
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,920
Saturn, Admiral Borsalino.

13
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,440
Please retreat. Hurry.

14
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:10,740
There's no time.

15
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:13,500
Kizaru and I will remain here.

16
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,300
Continue preparations without pause.

17
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:19,051
When you're through, commence bombardment.

18
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:21,820
Sir, you're sure?

19
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,080
Just go.

20
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:33,357
Yes sir you came to

21
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:34,817
kill me thought all

22
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,977
of this be over once you accomplish that?

23
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:42,157
Spare the island with or without me

24
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,917
egghead houses the latest research from

25
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,420
Every field of study in the world if
you burn it down you'll set scientific

26
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:52,380
progress back a century.

27
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:54,697
Revoke the Buster Call, now!

28
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:57,300
Please, Kizaru, help me.

29
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:05,378
What if there's something
else you're hiding from us?

30
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:08,032
Something troublesome for the government,

31
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:10,330
perhaps?

32
00:03:10,413 --> 00:03:12,637
That is a risk we would be fools to take.

33
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:15,600
We do not need your progress. Yes,

34
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:21,877
I'm begging you on

35
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:23,640
behalf of all humanity.

36
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:31,280
Ah, there's something
I neglected to mention.

37
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:38,920
It's about that ship that
escaped the island yesterday.

38
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:41,980
I've issued an order to have it pursued.

39
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:44,280
After all,

40
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:46,817
there might be people on board who learn

41
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:49,880
something about the Void
Sentry in their town.

42
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:56,780
I must ensure that none of them survive.

43
00:03:57,660 --> 00:04:00,160
So I sent a warship.

44
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:10,637
How could you do such a thing?

45
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,400
They don't know anything!

46
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:14,400
They're innocent civilians!

47
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:18,360
You are the one who got
them involved, Vegapunk.

48
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:24,900
You broke the law, just
as they did on Ohio.

49
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:35,420
You could not save your lust for knowledge,
so you dug too deep into the past.

50
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:50,860
As the beasts must remain on the
island, marines to your ships!

51
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:54,805
As soon as preparations are
complete, we'll commence our attack!

52
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,520
Ship 54, ready to fire!

53
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:59,280
Ship 21, ready to fire!

54
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:00,701
Awaiting orders!

55
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:08,990
Hurry!

56
00:05:09,073 --> 00:05:10,637
Everyone in the vacuum rocket!

57
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:14,257
We don't know how long Vegapunk
will be able to distract them.

58
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:17,752
The meeting point is the rear
entrance of the Labophase.

59
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:19,380
Be ready, okay?

60
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:21,657
We'll leave as soon as everyone arrives!

61
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:22,660
I got it!

62
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:25,600
Sanji, what about Vegapunk?

63
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:29,077
Don't you worry, Bonnie.

64
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:31,160
I'll get him out of here no sweat.

65
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:34,180
Good luck, bro, and stay safe!

66
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:36,280
I'll be fine.

67
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Hey, Nami, it's Sanji. What's your status?

68
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:46,197
We're already at the rear entrance.

69
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:48,162
What's all the noise down there?

70
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:49,900
Yeah, about that.

71
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:54,890
What?

72
00:05:54,973 --> 00:05:56,600
Did you say Buster Call?

73
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,820
This island is the force!

74
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:05,940
One Buster Call was
already too much for me.

75
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,160
This isn't fair.

76
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:11,560
What's going to happen to Stella?

77
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,957
Okay, this is no time to
be freaking out, guys!

78
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:17,746
Stay calm like me and
we'll all just run away!

79
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:18,920
Stop, Robin!

80
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:21,577
Everything's fine.

81
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:23,307
You just keep resting, okay?

82
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:26,400
Sanji, where's Luffy?

83
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:27,760
Is he with you?

84
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,697
What about Franky and Bonnie?

85
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:30,610
Are they okay?

86
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:33,757
Luffy's fine and the rest are headed up.

87
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:35,605
What's your status over there?

88
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:40,086
Most of us are good, but Zoro's
still getting held up by Luchi.

89
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,897
Jinbei is heading there now to go get him.

90
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:45,937
No way Zoro's finding his
way back without an escort.

91
00:06:46,020 --> 00:06:49,380
As for Brooke, he's supposed
to bring the Sunny around.

92
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:51,177
Lilith is there with him.

93
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:53,220
There's just one tiny problem.

94
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:56,857
We were going to have the Vega
Force One carry the ship away,

95
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:59,293
but that's not an option for us anymore.

96
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:02,160
Because Kizaru completely destroyed it.

97
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:05,837
Wait, then how are we supposed
to get off the island?

98
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:09,960
Well, I don't know, but
apparently Brooke has a plan.

99
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:17,297
Nothing like a piping hot cup of tea while

100
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:19,837
I effortlessly move our
ship over the island.

101
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:21,360
Am I good or what?

102
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:26,480
Not too shabby, Bones. Nice work.

103
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:30,949
At this rate, we'll hit the
rear entrance in no time at all.

104
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:38,542
Freezing the island clouds and letting the
ship slide on them was a work of genius.

105
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:44,468
Coming from the world's greatest genius,
I dare say, that is some high praise.

106
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,760
Damn, this is fun!

107
00:07:47,420 --> 00:07:50,040
So, how are we gonna
stop when we get there?

108
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:53,564
You know, I haven't thought
about that part yet.

109
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:55,590
What?!

110
00:07:57,460 --> 00:07:59,640
We're just gonna fall to our deaths!

111
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,580
Fix this right now!

112
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,977
I don't know how!

113
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,840
Help me, Lil' Head!

114
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:09,700
You better start thinking fast!

115
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:25,280
They still haven't brought
the Laplephase barrier down.

116
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:29,280
All ships, the target
is Egghead's urban area!

117
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:33,909
Concentrate fire on the central
factory and the future city.

118
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,240
Begin the bombardment!

119
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,300
Please wait!

120
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:54,226
We haven't got any seats yet!

121
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:02,140
The pacifists are firing! Run away!

122
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,000
Take it.

123
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:51,857
Preparing to depart febrile phase.

124
00:09:51,940 --> 00:09:53,440
Destination Lobby phase.

125
00:09:54,740 --> 00:09:55,677
Alright.

126
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:56,700
We're ready!

127
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:58,520
Vacuum rocket, go!

128
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:00,120
Let's do it!

129
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:08,340
That's what I call speed! Hell yeah!

130
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:12,320
Transit duration, 32 seconds.

131
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:28,400
Amano Murakumo, sword.

132
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:43,840
Damn it, Kizaru! Bonnie!

133
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:45,820
I'm on my way!

134
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:55,500
Pacifistas, fire on Bonnie and Kuma.

135
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:02,760
I want them dead.

136
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,380
Simply exquisite.

137
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:13,660
Kuma sacrificed everything
to save his daughter's life.

138
00:11:15,020 --> 00:11:19,760
And now she'll be blown to
bits by one of his own clones.

139
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:26,400
Truly the height of fire.

140
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:33,040
I'll feed him in for an insect.

141
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:42,960
Dad, it's me!

142
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:54,440
Bonnie, when I heard that
you had become a pirate,

143
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:58,480
the first possible scenario
flashed through my mind.

144
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:03,140
I could not control what the
Navy did with the Pacifistas,

145
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:05,340
built in your father's likeness.

146
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:12,000
He could be forced to shoot his own daughter
without understanding what he'd done.

147
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,140
By me!

148
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,497
No more...

149
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:23,286
Hey, that's Straw Hat, right?

150
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:28,277
Oh no, no more moving, Gumbarf!

151
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,360
Capture him!

152
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,128
He's an emperor of the sea!

153
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:43,280
They failed to destroy the escape vessel.

154
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:46,520
Someone alert! Kizaru!

155
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:02,980
Tell him, our attackers,
they're coming to Akainu!

156
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:10,580
Looks like the battle's on.

157
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:13,213
Guess the newspaper had that part right.

158
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:22,000
Did he just digest all of that food?

159
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:24,177
If we get too close, he might eat us.

160
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:26,495
I thought he was human, but maybe not.

161
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:30,870
Incoming!

162
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:35,760
We gotta move.

163
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:37,417
The flames are closing in on us.

164
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:40,088
If we stay here, then
we're going down, too.

165
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,180
Attack on three!

166
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:49,917
He may be strong, but
we'll stop him with C.

167
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:50,940
Prism Stonecum.

168
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:54,500
One, two...

169
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:58,820
Run to the ship! Go! No!

170
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:01,200
I had it down, boy!

171
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:05,400
Start from the shore
and burn it down! Fire!

172
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:14,080
Hold on, Gomorrah! Bunny!

173
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:18,220
Atlas! Come in! I need your help!

174
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,940
Shoot that fool!

175
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:24,760
And his daughter, too!

176
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:28,480
Listen to me.

177
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:29,875
You must tell Bonnie.

178
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:33,080
I'm almost there!

179
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:37,120
Okay!

180
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,340
I'm on it!

181
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:40,920
Bonnie!

182
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:43,420
Atmos!

183
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:52,740
Dad!

184
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,040
Don't shoot!

185
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,590
It's me!

186
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:58,480
We need to escape from here!

187
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:00,840
Please help us!

188
00:15:05,540 --> 00:15:06,370
Hey!

189
00:15:06,453 --> 00:15:07,437
What are you doing?

190
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:09,420
Did you hear that voice? What?

191
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:13,374
How in the hell can you hear
anything in all this noise?

192
00:15:23,620 --> 00:15:24,796
What are they doing?

193
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,593
Why'd they turn around?

194
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,800
All the precipices have gone wrong. No!

195
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:53,740
That single fear tugged at my mind.

196
00:15:57,420 --> 00:15:58,260
Bonnie

197
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:01,097
I was so worried.

198
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:05,200
What if you were killed by your own father

199
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:17,677
and kuma it's too cruel thinking that you

200
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:20,297
might harm your daughter
with your own hands.

201
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:24,460
That was a tragedy I could
not allow no matter what.

202
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:29,917
The government didn't
know but I programmed

203
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,557
something into every one of these weapons.

204
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:34,000
with Kuma's face.

205
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:36,620
So take heart.

206
00:16:37,020 --> 00:16:42,060
It doesn't matter if he's given a command
by the highest authority in the bird.

207
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:48,040
It doesn't matter if everyone
and everything is against him.

208
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:55,880
Bonnie, Kuma will always,
always be on your side.

209
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:01,400
I selfishly made my wish come true.

210
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:04,780
But I'm no fool.

211
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:09,240
I know how this would end.

212
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:13,460
Such decisions have
consequences after all.

213
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:18,180
They always do.

214
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,240
VEGAPUK!

215
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:28,520
Dammit, no!

216
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:30,440
VEGAPUK!

217
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:34,980
Kizaru, eliminate them immediately.

218
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:54,820
Kizaru! No!

219
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:57,341
This won't hurt, don't you worry.

220
00:17:57,840 --> 00:18:01,020
We'll cut you both in half
nice and clean. Darn it.

221
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:25,700
Wait, Strava?

222
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:27,180
Where is he?

223
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:31,270
Ha-ha-ha!

224
00:18:31,353 --> 00:18:33,400
Full belly, full power!

225
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:38,720
Ha-ha!

226
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,240
Now we're really having fun! Ha-ha!

227
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:45,940
Hey, Bonnie, you good?

228
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:50,260
Why is it bouncing like that?

229
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:51,518
Got a bigger issue!

230
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:54,160
I'm the path of faith!

231
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:07,750
VEGAPUNK!

232
00:19:09,340 --> 00:19:10,380
Say something!

233
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:13,720
We gotta go! Come on!

234
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:15,220
You can't die here!

235
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,360
I know that rhythm.

236
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:39,170
Nika?

237
00:19:39,860 --> 00:19:40,760
That's right.

238
00:19:40,940 --> 00:19:42,340
Nika is my hero.

239
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:46,327
When Nika comes, he'll smile and
laugh, moving to this rhythm.

240
00:19:56,380 --> 00:19:57,380
I see.

241
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:01,460
So you didn't realize the truth about him?

242
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:06,380
I couldn't be certain either,
till I saw it with my own eyes.

243
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:11,120
The very man Kuma placed his faith in,

244
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:17,220
Straw Hat moving, who he watched so
carefully, was Nika the sun gone all along.

245
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:25,340
Kuma had it right.

246
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:30,880
From the very start, the
Buster Call is futile.

247
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:38,480
Because there are people all over the
world who have been waiting for him.

248
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:41,400
They've waited for centuries.

249
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:47,432
Reporting from the northeast coast,
There is a massive ship approaching us!

250
00:20:47,740 --> 00:20:49,680
It's them, without a doubt.

251
00:20:49,980 --> 00:20:52,897
I thought they disbanded
over a hundred years ago.

252
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:54,620
Why are they here now?

253
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:57,900
Should we slow down? You kidding?

254
00:20:58,220 --> 00:20:59,280
Keep her steady.

255
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:05,120
They're coming right toward us! Fire!

256
00:21:12,940 --> 00:21:13,817
Damn it.

257
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:16,340
What the hell are the Giants doing here?

258
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:20,920
Oh, there they go again with
their why, why, why, Dory.

259
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:25,731
Don't they know everything that happens
in this world is inevitable, Froggy?

260
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:34,801
Don't worry, we're here
to back you up, Straw Hat.

261
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,940
Or should we call you Snake?

262
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:42,170
Emergency!

263
00:21:42,253 --> 00:21:43,083
Emergency!

264
00:21:43,166 --> 00:21:45,180
Agency, the giant pirates are here!

265
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:13,210
No, no,

266
00:22:13,293 --> 00:22:14,123
no,

267
00:22:14,206 --> 00:22:15,036
no,

268
00:22:15,119 --> 00:22:20,140
